# ---- Frequently Asked Questions ----
FAQ_INTRO = Answers to the most common questions. If yours isn't here, the log (toolbar) often helps.

FAQ_CAT_START = Getting started
FAQ_START_Q1 = How do I get started?
FAQ_START_A1 = Insert a floppy into A:. If Floppy Hub already knows it, it starts right away – if it's new, the app asks once.
FAQ_START_Q2 = What's the difference between the Motor and the app?
FAQ_START_A2 = The Motor (FloppyLauncher.exe) runs invisibly in the background and notices when a floppy is inserted. The app is the window you're looking at now – the two only talk over a short, purely local connection.
FAQ_START_Q3 = Does the app need to be open for floppies to start?
FAQ_START_A3 = No. The Motor keeps running on its own, even if the app window is closed.

FAQ_CAT_TRUST = Trust list
FAQ_TRUST_Q1 = What do "Start once" and "Always allow" mean?
FAQ_TRUST_A1 = For a program the app doesn't know yet, it asks once. "Start once" only applies to this floppy; "Always allow" remembers the path, arguments, and checksum for good.
FAQ_TRUST_Q2 = Why is C:\Windows blocked?
FAQ_TRUST_A2 = System folders stay blocked for safety, no matter what's on the trust list.
FAQ_TRUST_Q3 = How do I remove a permission again?
FAQ_TRUST_A3 = Options → Trust list → select the entry → "Remove permission".

FAQ_CAT_WRITE = Writing a floppy
FAQ_WRITE_Q1 = What does "Write" do?
FAQ_WRITE_A1 = It writes a game.txt to the floppy – for a Steam game, a program on the PC or the floppy, the hub menu, or the minigame. The app checks everything first and shows a preview.
FAQ_WRITE_Q2 = Why doesn't a freshly written floppy start right away?
FAQ_WRITE_A2 = On purpose: the app briefly remembers what it just wrote so the Motor doesn't accidentally start it immediately.

FAQ_CAT_LIBRARY = Library
FAQ_LIBRARY_Q1 = Where do the covers come from?
FAQ_LIBRARY_A1 = From Steam, loaded once and then cached locally – can be turned off in Options.
FAQ_LIBRARY_Q2 = Where is the library stored?
FAQ_LIBRARY_A2 = In library.csv, in the program folder – or under %LOCALAPPDATA%\FloppyHub if the program folder is read-only.

FAQ_CAT_DRIVES = Drives
FAQ_DRIVES_Q1 = Which drives does the app show?
FAQ_DRIVES_A1 = All removable media: floppies, USB sticks, memory cards, external hard drives, CD/DVD/Blu-ray – with connection, device name, serial number, and usage.
FAQ_DRIVES_Q2 = Which drives does the Motor watch?
FAQ_DRIVES_A2 = Always floppy A: – in Options you can add up to two more removable drives (e.g. a USB stick). Everything else never starts on its own, so nothing unexpected runs.

FAQ_CAT_CHAT = Chat
FAQ_CHAT_Q1 = How do I start a chat?
FAQ_CHAT_A1 = Type in a key, or load one from a floppy/USB stick – whoever types the same one lands in the same room. Without your own key, use the "Open Chat" instead.
FAQ_CHAT_Q2 = What is the Open Chat?
FAQ_CHAT_A2 = A permanent room without your own key, good for trying things out. Anyone with Floppy Hub can read along there – use your own key for private conversations.
FAQ_CHAT_Q3 = How do I switch to the local network?
FAQ_CHAT_A3 = Click "Local network" in the chat room. The others see a proposal with a Wi-Fi recommendation and can approve or decline – everyone needs to be on the same network.
FAQ_CHAT_Q4 = Switching to the local network doesn't work – why?
FAQ_CHAT_A4 = Usually because the devices are on different networks (the Wi-Fi recommendation in the proposal helps spot that). Sometimes the Windows Firewall, which asks once the first time.
FAQ_CHAT_Q5 = How do I save a contact?
FAQ_CHAT_A5 = Click a name in the members list → "Save as contact". Your own ID number stays the same across restarts.
FAQ_CHAT_Q6 = What does "(Admin)" in front of an ID mean?
FAQ_CHAT_A6 = That ID belongs to an admin of the open chat. The label cannot be faked: it is tied to the chat identity, and every message is signed with it.
FAQ_CHAT_Q7 = Can I be banned from the open chat?
FAQ_CHAT_A7 = Yes – for breaking the rules (e.g. offensive, racist or inappropriate content). A ban only applies to the open chat and is tied to your ID; private rooms with your own key are not affected. You then see nothing and cannot write – but you stay connected and are back automatically as soon as the ban runs out or the admin lifts it.

FAQ_CAT_GAME = Minigame
FAQ_GAME_Q1 = How do I play "Floppy Depot"?
FAQ_GAME_A1 = Push floppies into the marked slots with the arrow keys, Sokoban-style. Time, moves, and points count toward the leaderboard.
FAQ_GAME_Q2 = How do I create my own levels?
FAQ_GAME_A2 = Switch to the level editor in the minigame, paint, test, save. Every level gets its own ID – matching IDs let players compare.
FAQ_GAME_Q3 = Where do I see the leaderboard?
FAQ_GAME_A3 = In the chat room via the leaderboard button, or directly in the minigame.

FAQ_CAT_SETTINGS = Settings
FAQ_SETTINGS_Q1 = How do I change the language or look?
FAQ_SETTINGS_A1 = Options → Appearance/Language. The interface rebuilds right away, nothing needs restarting.
FAQ_SETTINGS_Q2 = How do I change autostart?
FAQ_SETTINGS_A2 = Run the setup again – it lets you turn autostart on or off without losing anything else.
FAQ_SETTINGS_Q3 = Where is my data stored?
FAQ_SETTINGS_A3 = Options → Motor shows the exact paths, with buttons to open them directly.
FAQ_SETTINGS_Q4 = How do I update Floppy Hub?
FAQ_SETTINGS_A4 = The app tells you itself when a newer version is out (at start, then every 45 minutes and whenever you open the window). "Update now" downloads the update automatically (the checksum is verified), installs it, and Floppy Hub restarts – settings and library are kept. Manually: Options → "Check for updates".

FAQ_CAT_TROUBLE = Troubleshooting
FAQ_TROUBLE_Q1 = Windows warns "Windows protected your PC" – what now?
FAQ_TROUBLE_A1 = The setup isn't signed yet. Click "More info" → "Run anyway".
FAQ_TROUBLE_Q2 = The floppy isn't recognized.
FAQ_TROUBLE_A2 = Check whether it's mounted as A: (Drives view) and whether the Motor is running (LED in Options). Some floppies take a moment to read.
FAQ_TROUBLE_Q3 = Where do I find error messages?
FAQ_TROUBLE_A3 = In the log (toolbar) – the same file as the console variant, lines colored by severity.

FAQ_CAT_PRIVACY = Privacy
FAQ_PRIVACY_Q1 = What leaves my computer?
FAQ_PRIVACY_A1 = Only chat – end-to-end encrypted over the free ntfy.sh service or the local network. Library, log, trust list, and settings stay on your own computer.
FAQ_PRIVACY_Q2 = Does chat save the history?
FAQ_PRIVACY_A2 = Nowhere, neither online nor locally. Only your own ID, contacts, bans issued by the admin in the open chat, and – if you choose – minigame records are kept.

